cases have been taken to preliminary design.
At the west end of the lake, Ayres looks forward to
designing features that will enhance the park, most
notably the flattened bank slopes. Where the 36-inch
and 42-inch storm sewers outfall into the lake, the
flattened bank will provide functional aesthetics to
the park where currently there is only a failing rock-
embedded concrete slope. The function will come
from an engineered boulder drop structure guiding
the overflow channel’s water to the lake level. The
aesthetics will come from riparian plantings that
thrive along a shoreline fringe.
In other areas along the north bank of the lake, the
banks are steep and the trail is right along the top of
the bank. In these areas the asphalt trail is crumbling
as the bank erodes beneath it. In these locations a
combination of flattening the bank and relocating the
trail will provide safety to pedestrians and reduce
park maintenance.
Valuable assets that Ayres brings to this project
include:
•
Traffic engineers
•
Storm drainage engineers
•
Extensive SWMM modeling experience
•
Hosting public meetings
•
Landscape architects
•
Extensive familiarity with Lake Minnehaha
and Holliday Park
Ayres is honored to have been selected as the
design engineer for the original Lake Minnehaha
Remediation Plan and the Phase 1 design that was
constructed last winter. Phase 1 corrected most
of the problems associated with Lake Minnehaha,
and last summer the lake looked better than it has
in more than 30 years. Phase 2 improvements will
ensure the lake remains pristine by eliminating two
of the causes of poor lake health. First, routing
the stormwater from the Duff Avenue storm sewer
into the lake will increase the circulation occurring
within the lake. Secondly, by providing water quality
treatment to all storm sewers discharging into the
lake sediment, oils and trash will no longer pollute
Lake Minnehaha. The Phase 2 improvements will be
the final step to keeping Lake Minnehaha a beautiful
lake in the heart of historic Holliday Park, and Ayres
would be honored to be able to see this project
through from beginning to end.
```

