C i t y o f C h e y e n n e L a k e M i n n e h a h a R e m e d i a t i o n P l a n
The City of Cheyenne retained Ayres Associates to develop a plan for ecological remediation of historic Lake
Minnehaha in Holliday Park. The lake has high phosphorus and nitrogen levels that promote eutrophic conditions
such as phytoplankton blooms, pH levels higher than most aquatic species can tolerate, water temperatures that
exclude cold water fish, odors that indicate anoxic conditions in the sediment, and limited depth. The remediation
plan addresses each of these issues. Tasks included water quality sampling, sediment sampling, locating a site
for disposal of dredged materials, environmental analysis, and preparation of the remediation plan.
